Q.3 What is the difference b/w bagging and boosting? 
|             | **Bagging**                                | **Boosting**                                   |
| ----------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Full form   | Bootstrap Aggregating                      | Boosting                                       |
| Main idea   | Train models **independently/in parallel** | Train models **sequentially**                  |
| Focus       | Mainly reduces **variance**                | Mainly reduces **bias**                        |
| Training    | Each model sees a different random sample  | Each new model focuses more on previous errors |
| Combining   | Usually **averaging/voting**               | Usually a weighted combination                 |
| Example     | Random Forest                              | XGBoost, AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting           |
| Overfitting | Generally less prone                       | Can overfit if not tuned properly              |
| Speed       | Can be parallelized                        | Sequential, so generally harder to parallelize |

